WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-24, with W14 (0.2.0)


STATE

  Version 0.2.0, Phase P3 IN PROGRESS (line editor complete), on branch
  dev. 0.2.0 adds:
  - interactive line editor in include/tam-clam/edit.h and
    src/edit/{buf.c,keymap.c,render.c,edit.c} on libtam's tam_tty,
    tam_key, and tam_uni, implementing arch/keys.md (following
    tamlinux/arch/keybindings.md);
  - UTF-8 and wide-character editing, multi-line editing (Alt+Enter and
    incomplete-syntax continuation), selection (Shift+Nav, Ctrl+A,
    Alt+M), clipboard ring + OSC 52 write (Ctrl+X/C/V, Alt+V),
    undo/redo (Ctrl+Z/Y), guidance overlay (Ctrl+G), widget palette
    (Ctrl+E), $VISUAL/$EDITOR (Alt+E), bracketed paste (CSI 200~/201~),
    SIGWINCH redraw, and the `bind` builtin;
  - child-process termios (VINTR=Ctrl+\, VQUIT disabled, VSUSP=Ctrl+P)
    with original termios restored on shell exit;
  - tests/test_edit.c unit tests, tests/pty/test_pty.c C PTY tests
    (xterm and TERM=linux), and sandbox/demo-0.2.0-edit.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; the Tamlinux-wide keybinding standard lives in
  tamlinux/arch/keybindings.md and tam-clam implements it in
  arch/keys.md (no vi mode, no built-in readline map, VINTR=Ctrl+\,
  VSUSP=Ctrl+P, Ctrl+F history search, Ctrl+Q quit); FUNCNEST sets the
  function recursion limit; signed 64-bit arithmetic overflow is a
  reported error; echo recognizes -n only and does not interpret
  backslash escapes by default.


